T09 LaTeX report draft build record (2026-11-07)

Scope: created a new report project under t09_report/ only. No prior stage
output, frozen model, prediction, T07/T08 artifact, source data, TASKS.md,
progress.md, verification.md, or test file was modified. Existing figures were
copied into t09_report/figures/; their originals remain in place. Report
content was sourced from the assignment guide, Stage 1 split summary, Stage 6
aggregate report/figure, active T06 non_tabpfn_v1 freeze report, T07 aggregate
report/tables, T08 manifest/submission contract, and T09 development SHAP
explanation. No row-level T07 prediction CSV or raw held-out rows were opened.

Commands run:
- mkdir -p t09_report/sections t09_report/figures logs
- cp stage6_catboost_outputs/model_comparison.png t09_report/figures/
- cp stage11_t07_outputs/development_{death_binary,zsn,fibr_preds}_raw_vs_platt_reliability.png,
  stage11_t07_outputs/{death_binary,zsn,fibr_preds}_reliability.png,
  stage13_t09_mortality_shap_outputs/mortality_shap_summary.png t09_report/figures/
- latexmk -pdf -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error -outdir=t09_report t09_report/main.tex
- gs -dSAFER -dBATCH -dNOPAUSE -sDEVICE=png16m -r110
  -sOutputFile=/tmp/t09_report_final_%02d.png t09_report/main.pdf
- .venv/bin/python -c "from pypdf import PdfReader; ..." (8-page/text/placeholder/figure/matrix checks)
- rg -n 'undefined|Warning|Overfull|Underfull|Citation' t09_report/main.log

The first LaTeX pass failed on a literal title escape; after correcting it,
the next pass exposed a missing amssymb import. Both were corrected in the new
report source. Final latexmk build completed successfully, producing an
8-page, 942,697-byte PDF. The final log contains no undefined references,
undefined citations, overfull/underfull box warnings, or LaTeX warnings.
Ghostscript rendered all eight pages at 110 dpi. Visual review covered every
rendered page, with close review of the updated held-out results page; tables,
figures, section transitions, and page numbering are legible and unclipped.
Text extraction confirmed six student-answer placeholders, four referenced
figures, no unresolved citation marker, and all three complete TN/FP/FN/TP
strings.

No model training, T07 evaluation, prediction generation, dependency install,
or test-label/prediction-row inspection was performed. Report limitations are
stated in the PDF, including the existing inability to prove exact row-level
X/y/ID correspondence from the saved test CSV artifacts. Six assignment
question answers and optional two-patient local SHAP explanations remain
student work. Independent review is pending.
